    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28-a1">

                <pb facs="0145" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg53"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McGinley to Mr.
                            Cridler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Athens, Greece</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that on June
                    10, 1899, I issued a passport to William Trauber, a naturalized citizen of the
                    United States residing temporarily in Roumania, taking in his old passport, No.
                    59, issued by the legation at Athens two years ago, and which I forwarded to the
                    Department with my last quartery returns. On July 5, 1899, the following
                    telegram was received at this consulate: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braila</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 4, 1899.</hi></p>
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">McGinley</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">American Consul, Athens:</hi></p>
                        <p>Austrian consul, Braila, refuses recognizing your passport. Considers
                            false document. Please take steps. Thanks.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Trauber.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>On July 6, 1899, I stated the case verbally to the chargé d’affaires of the
                    Austrian legation, Athens, showing him the telegram. He kindly informed me that
                    his legation had no control over the consuls in Roumania, but that he would
                    telegraph the consul at Braila that the passports issued by the United States
                    consul at Athens were good. I then wired Mr. Trauber as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 6, 1899.</hi></p>
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Trauber</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Braila:</hi></p>
                        <p>Austrian legation wires consul at Braila that my passports are good.
                            Write particulars immediately.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">McGinley.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0146" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/>
                <p>I now am in receipt of a letter from Mr. Trauber giving particulars, and I
                    inclose a true and correct copy of that letter.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your instructions, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William McGinley</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
